 ## Overview
-Software Cell-Projection Progressive Rendering is a software-based method for rendering Adaptive Mesh Refinement (AMR) data sets [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visualizing multi-resolution grids by allowing the contribution of coarser cells to be replaced with more accurate representations from finer hierarchy levels [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike its siblings, it explicitly supports progressive rendering through a pixel-level replacement mechanism, enabling interactive rates by dynamically adjusting traversal depth based on frame time [S1, S2, unofficial].
